<article class="help-article p-4">
    <header class="help-article-header mb-4">
        <span class="material-symbols-outlined help-article-icon">account_tree</span>
        <h1 class="help-article-title">Composite Types</h1>
        <p class="help-article-lead">
            Composite types define reusable value shapes that can be selected as attribute types.
        </p>
    </header>

    <h2 class="help-heading">Create a composite type</h2>
    <ol class="help-steps">
        <li><strong>Open the main menu</strong> and choose <em>Add Composite Type</em>.</li>
        <li><strong>Name the type</strong> in the Inspector.</li>
        <li><strong>Add elements</strong> in the center pane to describe the values that belong to the composite.</li>
    </ol>

    <h2 class="help-heading">Use it from an attribute</h2>
    <p>
        After creating a composite type, select an entity attribute and choose the composite type from
        the attribute Type menu. Singularity stores the selected composite type name as the attribute's
        value class.
    </p>

    <div class="help-callout">
        <span class="material-symbols-outlined">label</span>
        <div>
            <strong>Model shared value objects once.</strong>
            Composite types are useful for repeated shapes such as coordinates, money values, address
            fragments, or other structured values that should not become standalone entities.
        </div>
    </div>
</article>
